hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"202","This is Yusuf bin Musa, this is Jarir. H Muhammad ibn Rafi’ narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju’fi narrated to us, on the authority of Zaida, both of them, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara, he said: Al-Nazzal bin Sabra told me, he said: We prayed the noon prayer with Ali, then we went out to Al-Rahba. He said: “So he called for a vessel containing drink.” So he took it and gargled it. Mansour said: I think he said: He sniffed it, wiped his face, arms, head, and feet, then drank the remainder while he was “Standing,” then he said: “There are people who hate to drink while standing. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did the same as what I did,” and he said: This is the ablution of one who does not perform it.” This is the wording of the hadith of Zaydah."
